    "research": "PubMed E-utilities searches covered 30 fresh osteoporosis self-management topics, all classified as non-prescription-category candidates. The final query set returned 168 unique PubMed PMIDs, 168 article IDs requested, 168 fetched article records, and 166 abstracts available for inspection; two fetched records lacked abstracts. Retained numeric intervention-versus-control results or valid relative effects were verified for PMID records: 27766596, 17080541, 33237064, 29337906, 33469276, 28975661, 32176813, 35704055, 25058107, 19488681, 32543212, 34371870, 34936992, 31844906, 28107853, 31925473, 19194641, 30655662, 31454046, and 33990483. Twenty PubMed references were added across 20 new entries. New entries cover acupuncture, Baduanjin qigong, calcium with vitamin D, collagen peptides, high-intensity exercise, home resistance exercise, land exercise, magnesium, mindfulness with medical yoga, omega-3, patient education, Pilates, resistance and balance exercise, self-management education, Tai Chi, vitamin D, and yoga. Walking, Tai Chi, and whole-body vibration were linked to existing entries. Dance, fall prevention, physical therapy, telerehabilitation, cognitive behavioral therapy, heat therapy, and massage were screened because the selected records were protocols, prescription-drug combinations, or lacked direct topic-specific numeric or relative results. No build error or new targeted comparison/effect/line warning remained. One truthful unknown-sample-size warning and four truthful thin-study warnings were added by this batch.",
