    "research": "PubMed E-utilities searches covered 30 fresh chronic-low-back-pain self-management topics, all classified as non-prescription-category candidates. The final query set returned 153 unique PubMed PMIDs, 153 article IDs requested, 152 fetched article records, and 152 abstracts available for inspection; PMID 32338846 was returned by search but was not present in the fetched batch. Retained numeric intervention-versus-control results or valid relative effects were verified for PMID records: 35916848, 39375007, 38497906, 36958977, 31261549, 39485352, 40530198, 31103123, 27002445, 34398206, 33484240, 38805446, 38609994, 39048701, 40561080, 34994794, 36775506, 40938602, 36138055, 32434666, 34932756, 32434372, and 31309333. Twenty-three PubMed references were added across 23 new entries. New entries cover graded sensorimotor retraining, running, resistance exercise, stretching, walking, virtual yoga, tai chi and qigong, mindfulness, cognitive behavioral therapy, virtual-reality self-management, pain education, behavioral activation, manual therapy, telemedicine exercise, aquatic exercise, myofascial release, acupuncture, dry needling, heat with TENS, TENS, low-calorie diet, and probiotics. Pilates, low-level laser, spinal manipulation, cognitive functional therapy, omega-3, and vitamin D were linked to existing entries. The anti-inflammatory-diet topic was screened because the selected PMID 25237981 record described a physician-prescribed medical food rather than a retained non-prescription-category intervention. No build error or new targeted comparison/effect/line warning remained. Four truthful thin-study warnings remain for the 40-, 42-, 40-, and 48-participant trials.",
